In vanilla nethack, polymorph traps only disappear after they have
polymorphed the player, or if they have been destroyed by creating a
pit or trapdoor on the same square.  Wizards are particularly well
suited to repeatedly polymorphing their pets, because if you have
magic resistance you can step on the trap and then displace your pet
directly onto the trap, over and over until the pet becomes something
really kick-ass.  Sometimes the pet will polymorph into something that
cannot be polymorphed again, like a (baby) gray dragon or an arch-
lich.  It can be dangerous to leave a polymorph trap lying around, so
it is best to either engrave Elbereth and leave an object on top of
it, or push a boulder over it.

