Ok, I see.  You have a pathological fear of fountains.  Lets separate
myth from reality and understand the correct use of fountains:

See: http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/foun-343.html

Once you have luck >= 4, poison resistance, and enough hitpoints to
survive getting surrounded by water moccasins, it makes a lot of sense
to quaff from every fountain you find, except the ones in minetown.

The possible bad effects from fountains are ( 1 in 30 chance of each )
1) water moccasins - a few of these may be created - if you want to be
'safe' if this happens, engrave Elbereth on all eight squares
surrounding the fountain
2) Hostile water demon - if you want to be 'safe' if this happens,
engrave Elbereth on all eight squares surrounding the fountain
3) water nymph created if you want to be 'safe' if this happens,
engrave Elbereth on all eight squares surrounding the fountain
4) poisoned water - have poison resistance before you quaff from
fountains
5) Each item in your inventory has 1/5 chance of being cursed - Don't
carry/wear items that you don't want to risk getting cursed - esp. bag
of holding.
6) You lose gold - don't carry any gold in main inventory when
quaffing.
7) you vomit and hunger is increased

Possble good effects from fountains:
1) Stat boost (to all stats if luck>3) - 1/7 chance per fountain
2) See invisible - 1/30 chance per quaff
3) Water demon gives wish - small chance, better on upper levels of
the dungeon.
4) You see your attributes - enlightenment - 1/30 chance per quaff
5) You find a gem - 1/30 chance
6) temporary scare monster - 1/30 chance

Dipping items in a fountain will never give the 'curse inventory'
effect.  You can safely smash a fountain with a pickaxe to make pools
to blank scrolls and dilute potions with no risk of negative effects.

